{
  "text": "AI assistants have started shopping for people. But PayPal's agent checkout is built for merchants with a website store. Rosa bakes from her kitchen. She has no website, just this sheet of paper. One home baker in Virginia took orders in texts and DMs, then tracked them on a spreadsheet. In a 2016 Census survey, nearly half of US food and lodging employer firms had no website. An assistant can't order from a sheet of paper.",
